### 38

- **Rule:** Model types that **design-system components take as parameters** (payloads, slot specs, text models, image shape, enum variants) with **`@Immutable`** when all public state is deeply immutable, or **`@Stable`** when the type holds **mutable composition state** (e.g. `MutableState`, lambdas) or a Stable-appropriate contract; put annotations on the **sealed interface / enum / data class** used with the component.
- **Why it exists:** Skipping `Immutable` / `Stable` makes Compose treat types as **unstable** and weakens recomposition wins; [design-system AGENTS.md](../../../client/core/design-system/src/commonMain/kotlin/dev/kigya/headway/core/designSystem/AGENTS.md) already requires `ImmutableList` for collection fields in immutable models.
- **Bad pattern (short):** Public `data class FreudWideNavigationItem(...)` or sealed slot types passed into `Freud*` composables without compose-runtime stability markers.
- **Correct pattern (short):** `@Immutable data class FreudWideNavigationItem`; `@Stable sealed interface FreudTopBarStartSlot` when implementations carry `onClick` lambdas; `@Stable class FreudAnimationTrigger` for mutable trigger state; enums used as DS parameters annotated `@Immutable`.

